1
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:08,170
OK.

2
00:00:08,170 --> 00:00:10,640
If you want to adopt an animal,

3
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:12,950
first we need to know some references.

4
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:14,740
References?

5
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:16,490
People we know?

6
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:19,190
Friends, teachers....

7
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:21,560
We need to talk to some people about you.

8
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:23,830
We want to be sure that you're responsible

9
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:26,580
and that you can take good care of an animal.

10
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:28,460
Then you have to fill out this form

11
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:31,020
about your family background.

12
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:32,240
Is that it?

13
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,350
No, there's more.

14
00:00:34,350 --> 00:00:37,970
We need to know about your history with animals.

15
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:39,530
Have you ever owned an animal?

16
00:00:39,530 --> 00:00:41,090
Yes.

17
00:00:41,090 --> 00:00:43,490
We had a cat when I was eight years old.

18
00:00:43,490 --> 00:00:45,050
I love cats.

19
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:47,110
Do you have any animals now?

20
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:49,400
Unfortunately, no.

21
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:50,870
Anything else?

22
00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:52,520
We also like to know

23
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:54,300
your reasons for wanting an animal.

24
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,820
Just to hold it and cuddle with it.

25
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:58,310
Just to have as a pet.

26
00:00:58,310 --> 00:01:01,500
I love animals.

27
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:04,710
To have a friend -- a pal.

28
00:01:04,710 --> 00:01:08,400
You know, man's best friend is his dog.

29
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,620
And one thing more.

30
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:11,430
If you're under twenty-one years of age ...

31
00:01:11,430 --> 00:01:12,370
That's me.

32
00:01:12,370 --> 00:01:14,070
Then an adult must sign for you.

33
00:01:14,070 --> 00:01:15,690
Uh-oh.

34
00:01:15,690 --> 00:01:16,950
No problem.

35
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:19,320
My parents will think it's a good idea.

36
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:20,550
I'll be back with them.

37
00:01:20,550 --> 00:01:24,000
If the real owners don't come to claim Gemma ...

38
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,540
After forty-eight hours.

39
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:27,980
But please call first.

40
00:01:27,980 --> 00:01:31,420
Thanks for your information and for being so helpful.

41
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:32,680
It's my pleasure.

42
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,290
Nice talking to both of you.

43
00:01:34,290 --> 00:01:35,060
Thanks again.

44
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:37,900
Bye.

45
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:40,660
Maybe the real owners will come to claim her.

46
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:42,470
Her eyes look so sad.

47
00:01:42,470 --> 00:01:44,040
She must really miss them.

48
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:45,980
I see you're both animal lovers.

49
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,180
We are.

50
00:01:47,180 --> 00:01:48,390
Good-bye, Miss Aborn.

51
00:01:48,390 --> 00:01:49,810
We'll call in a couple of days.

52
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:53,060
Good-bye, and thanks for bringing Gemma in.

53
00:01:53,060 --> 00:02:03,700
Bye.

54
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:06,690
I keep thinking about the dog -- about Gemma,

55
00:02:06,690 --> 00:02:08,540
alone in the animal shelter.

56
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:10,550
I know.

57
00:02:10,550 --> 00:02:12,040
But I promise you, Alexandra,

58
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,790
the dog is just fine.

59
00:02:13,790 --> 00:02:16,040
They're very kind to the animals.

60
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:16,810
I know they are.

61
00:02:16,810 --> 00:02:19,670
I mean about her being alone.

62
00:02:19,670 --> 00:02:21,180
Even if they are kind to Gemma,

63
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:24,060
she's still alone, without her family.

64
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,530
Ready, folks?

65
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:26,840
Are you ready, Alexandra?

66
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:28,480
Yes, I'm ready.

67
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:31,390
I'll have the chef's salad, please.

68
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:34,700
I will have a cheeseburger, medium rare,

69
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:37,870
with raw onion, and french fries, please.

70
00:02:37,870 --> 00:02:39,000
Anything to drink?

71
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,280
A diet cola, please.

72
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:43,630
Ginger ale with lots of ice for me, thank you.

73
00:02:43,630 --> 00:02:44,400
I've got it.

74
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,850
Thanks.

75
00:02:46,850 --> 00:02:48,020
Aren't you surprised

76
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:49,800
that the animal shelter is so careful

77
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:51,690
about finding homes for the animals?

78
00:02:51,690 --> 00:02:53,720
No, I'm not.

79
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:55,550
And a cheeseburger, medium rare,

80
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:57,590
with onion and french fries.

81
00:02:57,590 --> 00:03:00,830
And a ginger ale with lots of ice.

82
00:03:00,830 --> 00:03:03,600
Salad dressing?

83
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,820
Hey, I wanted you to hear my new sound system

84
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:08,370
when the dog scratched on the front door.

85
00:03:08,370 --> 00:03:09,340
Let's finish eating,

86
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:11,870
and then we'll go back to my house.

87
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:13,570
I want you to hear my new tapes.

88
00:03:13,570 --> 00:03:35,510
I've got some great new dance music.

89
00:03:35,510 --> 00:03:36,070
Hello.

90
00:03:36,070 --> 00:03:37,490
Stewart residence.

91
00:03:37,490 --> 00:03:37,930
Hello.

92
00:03:37,930 --> 00:03:39,390
Is Robbie Stewart there?

93
00:03:39,390 --> 00:03:40,000
This is he.

94
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,020
Who's this?

95
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:43,980
This is Linda Aborn from the animal shelter.

96
00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:46,750
It's Linda from the animal shelter.

97
00:03:46,750 --> 00:03:47,750
Yes, Linda.

98
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:48,880
Hi.

99
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:51,010
We have good news and bad news, Robbie.

100
00:03:51,010 --> 00:03:52,040
Oh?

101
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:54,350
The good news is that the Levinsons have come by

102
00:03:54,350 --> 00:03:55,650
to pick up the dog.

103
00:03:55,650 --> 00:03:59,500
The bad news is, you won't be able to adopt the dog.

104
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:01,050
That's OK.

105
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:03,970
Come by one day and look at some of the other dogs.

106
00:04:03,970 --> 00:04:05,860
I'm sure there's one for you.

107
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:06,810
Thanks, Robbie.

108
00:04:06,810 --> 00:04:10,370
And the Levinsons thank you for bringing their dog to us.

109
00:04:10,370 --> 00:04:11,790
Thanks, Linda.

110
00:04:11,790 --> 00:04:21,200
Bye.

111
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,020
The owners claimed Gemma?

112
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:24,620
That's right.

113
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:26,890
I'm glad for the dog.

114
00:04:26,890 --> 00:04:29,180
I guess I am, too.

115
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:30,350
She said if I come by,

116
00:04:30,350 --> 00:04:35,050
she'll help me find another dog.

117
00:04:35,050 --> 00:04:38,050
Come on. Let's dance.
